Market Challenges
High Development and Certification Costs – Engineering explosion-proof devices requires expensive specialized materials and rigorous testing. Manufacturers must invest significantly in research and certification processes, with ATEX/IECEx compliance adding approximately 20-35% to product development costs.
Technical Complexity in Hazardous Area Classification – Proper deployment requires thorough understanding of zone classifications (Zone 0/1/2 or Div 1/2) which vary by region and application. Misclassification can lead to either dangerous under-specification or unnecessary over-engineering of equipment.
Training and Awareness Gaps – Many facilities in developing regions continue using standard air samplers in hazardous areas due to insufficient understanding of explosion risks and protection methods.

